        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Vogue, Y'all, Mademoiselle\n- Places: United States, Oxford, Mississippi, American South\n- People: Mary Cantwell\n- Topics: magazine publishing, circulation, Southern coverage\n\nFacts:\n- Vogue began as a weekly newspaper in the United States in 1892 and became a monthly publication years later.\n- Y'all is an American magazine based in Oxford, Mississippi, in the American South.\n- Y'all was published bimonthly with a circulation of 100,000.\n- Y'all features Southern celebrities, events, and ordinary people with extraordinary stories.\n- According to its MySpace page, Y'all covers the South's 15 states and 103 million people.\n- Mary Cantwell wrote for Mademoiselle and Vogue during her career.",
